rom `MCP_PORT` (`7411` when unset) on\n  `127.0.0.1`; `GET /healthz` polled until it answers `200`, at most 5 seconds;\n  failure names the polled address.\n- **session** — `POST {\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"initialize\"}` to `/mcp`\n  with `Content-Type: application/json`; the reply's status and headers are kept\n  on `State.Response` for later steps; a Then step with no reply fails.\n- **ticket** — `X-Session-Ticket` of the last reply, 32 lowercase hex chars on a\n  200 reply; failure names the status and the header value.\n- **protocol version** — `X-MCP-Protocol` of the last reply, a `YYYY-MM-DD`\n  date; failure names what the reply carried.\n\n## Required Changes\n\n### Change #1: Create the suite's step definitions and its `Register` function\n\n**File:** `tests/mcp/steps/steps.go`\n\n**Action:** Use the **Write** tool to create this new file with exactly the\ncontent below. (No `old_string` — the file does not exist. Everything goes in\none new file; `Register` is the single registration function the harness calls,\nand all four definitions are registered inside it.)\n\n**Content:**\n\n```go\npackage steps\n\nimport (\n\t\"bytes\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"net/http\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"regexp\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"time\"\n)\n\n// defaultMCPPort is the port the MCP server listens on when MCP_PORT is unset.\nconst defaultMCPPort = \"7411\"\n\n// healthTimeout bounds how long \"the MCP server is running\" waits for readiness.\nconst healthTimeout = 5 * time.Second\n\n// healthPollInterval paces the readiness poll.\nconst healthPollInterval = 50 * time.Millisecond\n\n// initializeRequest is the JSON-RPC 2.0 request that opens a session.\nconst initializeRequest = `{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"initialize\"}`\n\n// ticketPattern is the shape of a granted ticket: 32 lowercase hex characters.\nvar ticketPattern = regexp.MustCompile(`^[0-9a-f]{32}$`)\n\n// protocolPattern is the shape of a named protocol version: a YYYY-MM-DD date.\nvar protoc